Note on what this replaces: the repository previously carried the MIT licence
that `create-expo-app` scaffolds in, with the copyright still reading
"650 Industries, Inc. (aka Expo)". That licence was never meant to cover this
project's own code, and MIT would have granted anyone the right to use and sell
it. Reinstate an open licence deliberately, if ever — not by leaving a template
file in place.

Third-party dependencies keep their own licences; see package.json and
krushimitra-backend/requirements.txt.
